---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Now — Shubham" description="What Shubham is focused on right now.">
  <Header />

  <main>
    <div class="page-head rv">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>
      <h1>Now</h1>
    </div>

    <article class="now-text rv">
      <p>
        Finishing my 4th semester at <strong>IIITM Gwalior</strong>. The coursework load is manageable this term — mostly electives — which means I have real time to build things.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working on <strong>Merix v2</strong> — currently fixing the matching pipeline. The scoring layer blends semantic similarity with structured signals, and getting the weights right on the structured side is taking more iteration than I expected. The explanation generation is working well though; the pipeline produces honest, readable reasons for every rank.
      </p>

      <p>
        Reading <strong>Designing Data-Intensive Applications</strong> — chapter 7 right now, on transactions. The storage engine chapter (3) was the highlight so far. I'm taking notes in public, which means I actually have to understand things before writing them down.
      </p>

      <p>
        Writing about <strong>RAG systems</strong> — specifically the failure modes nobody documents. Platewise taught me more about what breaks than what works, and I think that's the more useful thing to share. Drafting a post on why embedding similarity alone produces terrible ranking results.
      </p>

      <p>
        Grinding <strong>Codeforces</strong> toward 1900. Stuck around 1847 for a few weeks — the jump from Expert to Candidate Master is real. Solving more 1800-2000 rated problems and reviewing editorial approaches I wouldn't have thought of.
      </p>

      <p class="closing">
        Looking for <strong>Summer 2027 internships</strong> in backend engineering or AI. If you're hiring someone who ships, writes, and reads without being told to — <a href="mailto:shubham@example.com">get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 0;
  }

  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }

  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .72rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: .05em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .now-text p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .now-text strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .now-text a {
    color: var(--accent2);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color .15s;
  }

  .now-text a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .closing {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
